# Line endings are part of the project's byte-exact contract: every golden
# under tests/ is compared byte for byte against the engine's LF output, and
# the .part / .cam files are parsed by the same engine. Pin LF in the working
# tree on every platform, so a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true does
# not hand the tests CRLF goldens (found on the 2026-10-03 move from WSL to
# native Windows: 115 integration tests red, all of them this). `text=auto`
# leaves files git detects as binary alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
